####
# DocuFlow environment configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `npm run dev` and `npm start` load `.env` if it is
# present; deployments set the same variables through their own mechanism.
#
# This file is the register of record for every variable the repository reads —
# the server's, the release scripts', and the test harness's. The server's are
# read in `server/config.ts` and nowhere else, which refuses to boot when a
# required one is missing. docs/CONFIGURATION.md explains each in prose.
#
# ADR-0018: this repository is a parallel environment. Never put a production
# credential, production URL, or production dataset in it — not even briefly.
# Every account named here is a fresh one provisioned for this effort.
####

# ─── Database (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Either DATABASE_URL, or every PG* variable instead. DATABASE_URL wins.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/docuflow
# PGHOST=localhost
# PGPORT=5432
# PGUSER=docuflow
# PGPASSWORD=change-me
# PGDATABASE=docuflow_dev
# Owner/migrator URL when DATABASE_URL is the application role (no BYPASSRLS).
# Unset: migrate uses DATABASE_URL. #97.
# DATABASE_MIGRATE_URL=postgresql://owner:password@host:5432/docuflow

# node-postgres instead of the Neon serverless driver — needed for a database
# Neon's WebSocket driver cannot reach, such as a local or CI Postgres.
# DB_DRIVER=pg

# ─── Sessions (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs session cookies. Any long random string; rotating it logs everyone out.
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# ─── Desktop access-token signing key (required) ─────────────────────────────
# Signs the hour-long tokens the desktop agent presents, written as
# <key-id>:<secret>. The id names the key and travels in every token it signs;
# the secret is 32+ random bytes, e.g. openssl rand -hex 32, and boot refuses one
# under 32 characters. There is no generated fallback: a key invented at boot
# would be gone at the next one, and every signed-in agent with it, so boot stops
# instead of signing the fleet out.
JWT_SECRET=2026-08:change-me-to-a-long-random-string
# Set only during a rotation: while it is here, tokens signed with either key
# verify and new ones carry the current key's id. Clear it one token lifetime
# (1 hour) after the last replica picked the new key up — docs/CONFIGURATION.md
# has the procedure.
# JWT_PREVIOUS_SECRET=2026-05:the-previous-32-plus-character-secret

# ─── Evidence export (the backup job's environment only) ─────────────────────
# Read by scripts/evidence-export.ts and by nothing the server runs. These
# belong in the nightly job's environment and nowhere else: ADR-0016 makes the
# standalone AWS account an evidence copy the main environment cannot alter, and
# a credential this app could read is a copy this app could alter (#57).
#
# 64 hex characters, openssl rand -hex 32. Held outside AWS on purpose, so that
# possession of the bucket is not possession of the database. Lose it and every
# locked export is unreadable — and compliance mode means they cannot be deleted
# either, only paid for until their retention expires.
# EVIDENCE_EXPORT_KEY=
# The S3 bucket in the standalone account. Only used to print the upload
# command; nothing here uploads.
# EVIDENCE_S3_BUCKET=

# ─── Object storage (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bucket roots, written as /<bucket>/<prefix>. The private root holds uploads and
# evidence; the first public search path receives public uploads.
PRIVATE_OBJECT_DIR=/my-bucket/.private
PUBLIC_OBJECT_SEARCH_PATHS=/my-bucket/public

# One of the next two is required: signed URLs need a key that can sign, so the
# identity must be a service account, and boot refuses an environment naming
# neither. The boot line reports which of the two is in use.
#
# The key file's JSON — verbatim on one line, or base64-encoded, which survives
# secret stores that mangle the newlines inside private_key.
GCS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY=
# Or a path to that same key file, read by the Google SDK rather than by this app.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json
# Only needed when the key file omits it.
# GCS_PROJECT_ID=

# ─── HTTP server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# development | production | test. Defaults to development; the production build
# replaces it with a literal, so it is set by the runtime, rarely by hand.
# NODE_ENV=development
# PORT=5000
# Absolute base URL this deployment is reached at, used for links in outbound
# email. Defaults to http://localhost:5000.
# APP_URL=https://docuflow.example.com

# ─── Process role (optional — HTTP unless this is the Worker) ────────────────
# http (default) serves the app and never claims Jobs. worker claims and runs them.
# DOCUFLOW_ROLE=http
# HTTP setInterval dispatchers (due reminders, stale timers, daily nudge).
# Default on until the Worker is proven. 0 / false / off disable them.
# DOCUFLOW_HTTP_BACKGROUND_INTERVALS=1

# ─── Email (optional — sends fail and report why while unset) ────────────────
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Verified sender. Defaults to DocuFlow <noreply@resend.dev>.
# RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=DocuFlow <noreply@example.com>

# ─── Stripe billing (optional — Checkout fails closed while unset) ───────────
# Test-mode secret. Unset is supported: Entitlement reads still work for
# Workspaces with no Stripe objects (the seeded Workspace). Checkout fails closed.
# Never a production Stripe account (ADR-0018).
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_
# Stripe Price id for Plan `pro`. Mapped only inside the adapter; not a DocuFlow price.
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=price_

# ─── Clerk identity (optional — IdentityProvider fails closed while unset) ───
# Test-mode secret. Unset is supported: HTTP still authenticates with
# email/password and Replit OIDC. IdentityProvider operations fail closed.
# Never a production Clerk instance (ADR-0018).
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_
# The Phase 5 dual-auth drain (#109). Off — the default — is legacy auth only.
# On, a Clerk session enters the Workspace alongside the legacy one for the same
# User; turning it back off is the rollback. Temporary; owner @Lamakira, removed
# with Replit OIDC and MCP_API_KEY (#111).
# DOCUFLOW_IDENTITY_DUAL_AUTH=on

# ─── Telemetry (optional — instrumented always, exported only when asked) ────
# Where OpenTelemetry sends what it collects: none | console | otlp. Unset, the
# environment decides — nothing under test, the console in development, nothing
# in production until an endpoint below is set. `none` still instruments the
# process, so its log lines carry the trace id of the request they came from;
# only NODE_ENV=test leaves it unpatched. docs/OBSERVABILITY.md explains what is
# collected and the IDs-only rule every field has to satisfy.
# OTEL_EXPORTER=console
# The collector's root URL; each signal appends its own /v1/traces, /v1/metrics,
# /v1/logs. Setting it selects the OTLP exporter. ADR-0018: boot refuses a
# collector that is not on this machine unless ALLOW_REMOTE_OTLP=1.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# ALLOW_REMOTE_OTLP=1
# Sent with every OTLP request — where a hosted collector's ingest token goes.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=authorization=Bearer change-me,x-source=docuflow
# Names this process in every signal. The Phase 3 worker runs the same image
# under a different one. Defaults to docuflow-server.
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=docuflow-server
# How often metrics are exported. Defaults to 60000.
# OTEL_METRIC_EXPORT_INTERVAL_MS=60000

# ─── AI and transcription (optional — each feature fails while unset) ────────
# Embeddings, retrieval-augmented chat, and audio transcription.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Fathom transcripts; without it the scraper falls back to the browser path.
# FATHOM_API_KEY=
# The browser that scraper launches. Unset is the normal state: Playwright opens
# the build `npx playwright install chromium` put in place, which is what the
# image installs too. Set it only on a host carrying a browser of its own — a
# value with nothing runnable at it fails the scrape in this variable's name,
# and leaves the rest of the server alone (#37).
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_PATH=

# ─── Desktop releases (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer token the release pipeline presents to POST /api/internal/desktop-releases.
# DESKTOP_RELEASE_CI_TOKEN=
# Bucket the desktop installers are published to, for scripts/release-desktop.mjs
# and scripts/upload-to-gcs.mjs.
# INSTALLER_GCS_BUCKET=
# The deployment scripts/release-desktop.mjs registers the release against. It
# has no default: naming the target every time is what keeps a release run from
# reaching a deployment nobody meant to publish to (ADR-0018).
# DOCUFLOW_API_URL=https://docuflow.example.com
# The GitHub repository and workflow scripts/release-desktop.mjs builds the
# installers on. Both default to this project's own; override to build elsewhere.
# GH_REPO=owner/repository
# GH_WORKFLOW=desktop-release.yml

# ─── MCP (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin-impersonation key accepted as X-API-Key. Phase 5 removes it.
# MCP_API_KEY=

# ─── Tests (optional — read by the harness, not by the server) ───────────────
# The database `npm test` runs against. It is truncated between tests, so it must
# be disposable. Defaults to the docker-compose.test.yml Postgres on 5433.
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/docuflow_test
# The harness refuses a non-local TEST_DATABASE_URL unless this is 1 (ADR-0018).
# Set it only for a remote test database holding nothing you want to keep.
# ALLOW_REMOTE_TEST_DB=1

# ─── Snapshot rehearsal (optional — read by scripts/snapshot-rehearsal.ts) ───
# `npm run snapshot:check` and `snapshot:scrub` refuse to run inside a Replit
# development workspace: ADR-0021 places those outside the published geography,
# and a restored production snapshot may not be loaded into one. Set this only
# for a database holding synthetic data (#53).
# ALLOW_DEVELOPMENT_REHEARSAL=1

# ─── Replit OIDC login (optional — removed in Phase 5) ───────────────────────
# REPL_ID=
# ISSUER_URL=https://replit.com/oidc
# Set by the Replit runtime, not by hand. They stand in for APP_URL when it is
# unset, so a Replit deployment keeps producing the links it always did; they
# leave with the OIDC login in Phase 5.
# REPLIT_DOMAINS=my-app.replit.app
# REPLIT_DEV_DOMAIN=my-app.replit.dev
